under its own applicable licences and notices. Obtain permission from its
actual rights holders where its existing licence does not authorize your use.
See THIRD_PARTY_SOURCE.md and the inventory in LICENSE-BOUNDARY.md.

## 2. App use is permitted; code reuse and republication require permission

### 2.1 Permission for everyone to use official app releases

ZHINFINITY grants everyone a nonexclusive, worldwide, royalty-free permission
to download, install, update, and run official, unmodified Mpv∞ app releases
distributed by ZHINFINITY or an expressly authorized distributor, on devices
they own or are authorized to use. This includes the copies reasonably
necessary to install, operate, update, and back up the app for their own use.
Ordinary app use is permitted for personal, educational, organizational, and
commercial purposes. No individual permission request is required for these
activities. These terms do not restrict media or data merely used with the app.

This end-user permission is for using the app, not for reusing its source code,
making derivative apps, sharing copies with others, rehosting APKs, or publishing
the app or a modified version in an app store or elsewhere. Sharing a link to
an official download is allowed; redistributing the app itself is not granted
by this section. Sections 4 and 5 preserve independently applicable rights.

### 2.2 Prior written permission for code reuse and republication

Except for section 2.1 and the rights preserved in sections 4 and 5, no licence
is granted to copy, reproduce, modify, adapt, create derivative works from,
reuse, redistribute, sublicense, sell, monetize, publish, upload, or otherwise
make available any Covered Material, in whole or in part, in source or binary
form. Each such activity requires prior written permission from ZHINFINITY.

This requirement applies to commercial and noncommercial activities alike,
including copying source code for private projects, reposting, app-store
publication, advertising-supported distribution, and incorporation into another
project. Public access, attribution, absence of a fee, or a failure to respond
to a request is not permission. The app-use grant in section 2.1 does not grant
general source-code reuse or republication rights.

Any permission must expressly identify the material and authorized activities
and their scope; section 2.1 itself provides that permission for ordinary app
use. No permission grants rights outside its scope or rights owned by others.
No separate patent, trademark, branding, or endorsement rights are granted by
these terms beyond any rights necessarily implied by the express app-use grant.

## 3. Attribution and no false authorship

Any use authorized under these terms must preserve applicable copyright,
author, licence, and third-party notices, and identify modifications and their
authors without presenting the original work as their own. You must not falsely
claim to be the original creator or author of material created by others, or
suggest that ZHINFINITY endorses your version without written authorization.
Attribution does not replace the permission required by section 2. These
conditions do not purport to impose new restrictions on previously licensed
material or independently licensed third-party material.
Ordinary app users do not need to publish a separate attribution statement;
leaving the app's built-in notices intact satisfies this section for their use.

